AIM
To write and execute Python programs to demonstrate different types of inheritance in Python, namely:
Hierarchical Inheritance – A single parent class is inherited by multiple child classes.
Single Inheritance – One child class inherits the properties and methods of a parent class.
Multilevel Inheritance – A class inherits from another derived class, forming a chain of inheritance.
Multiple Inheritance – A child class inherits properties and methods from more than one parent class


ALGORITHM
Program 1: Hierarchical Inheritance
Start the program
Create a parent class A with a method display().
Create two child classes B and C that inherit from class A.
Define separate methods show() in class B and show1() in class C.
Create a class D that inherits from both B and C.
Define a method result() in class D.
Create an object of class D.
Call all the inherited and defined methods using the object.
Stop the program.


Program 2: Single Inheritance
Start the program.
Create a parent class PARENT with two attributes, Asset1 and Asset2.
Define a method parentMtd() to display the parent class assets.
Create a child class child that inherits from PARENT.
Define an additional attribute Asset3 and a method childMtd() in the child class.
Create an object of the child class.
